<header><a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/pull/391">Sports Edge Lab <span> · College football</span></a><span>V097 actual return<br>V098 preparation review</span></header>
<div id="error" class="error" role="alert" hidden></div>
<main id="report" hidden>
<nav aria-label="Report sections"><a href="#actual">Actual work</a><a href="#research">What changed</a><a href="#leaders">Selected results</a><a href="#cpu">CPU evidence</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a><a href="#next">Next work</a><a href="#custody">Verified return</a></nav>
<div class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">306 jobs complete · Evidence preserved</p><h1>More ablations.<br>The validation leaders held.</h1><p class="lead">V097 finished its XGBoost and CatBoost source-ablation tranche. It added 204 policy variants while preserving the earlier 936 completed jobs. None of the nine primary leaders changed, and all five validation-weight profiles retain their previous winners.</p></div><aside class="status"><p class="eyebrow">Observed child and supervisor exit 0</p><h3>Operationally finished.<br>Scientifically partial.</h3><p id="closure-note"></p></aside></div>
<div class="metrics"><article class="metric"><span>New base-model fits</span><strong id="new-fits"></strong><p>Plus 294 calibrator fits; 12 exact fitted states reused.</p></article><article class="metric"><span>Registered jobs completed</span><strong id="complete-jobs"></strong><p>204 validation jobs and 102 frozen-test jobs.</p></article><article class="metric"><span>Peak concurrent fits</span><strong id="fit-processes"></strong><p>19 in validation, 22 in test; 24 workers admitted per phase.</p></article><article class="metric"><span>Known completed test games</span><strong id="test-games"></strong><p>All 1,309 policies score this known completed-game population.</p></article></div>
<div class="notice warn">The finished tranche remains a T-120 frozen reconstruction. Primary T-60 research, complete official/postseason coverage and other V13 requirements are unfinished. No production replacement or website deployment is established by this report.</div>

<section id="actual"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Observed owner execution</p><h2>The registered tranche finished</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><h3>Invocation and cumulative evidence</h3><dl class="facts" id="actual-facts"></dl><p class="fine" id="actual-clock"></p></article><article class="card"><h3>Completed work was reused</h3><dl class="facts" id="reuse-facts"></dl><p class="fine">A registered job, a new base fit, a calibrator fit, a reused state and a forecast row are separate counts. Re-emitted or rescored rows do not become newly issued historical forecasts.</p></article></div></section>

<section id="research"><p class="eyebrow">02 / New scientific evidence</p><h2>204 new variants; zero leader replacements</h2><p class="muted">The saved validation lock compares 1,309 policies. Each displayed new-family representative was selected by the 50/50 annual validation score within that new family and objective. Its 2026 value is reporting only. Its rank is against the full eligible comparison, not just the new tranche.</p>
<div class="controls"><label>New source-ablation family<select id="new-family" aria-label="New source-ablation family"><option>XGBoost</option><option>CatBoost</option></select></label></div>
<div class="card"><div class="table-wrap"><table class="leader-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Objective</th><th scope="col">New variant</th><th scope="col" class="num">50/50 rank</th><th scope="col" class="num">Validation score</th><th scope="col" class="num">Sources absent · validation</th><th scope="col" class="num">2026 report</th></tr></thead><tbody id="new-family-rows"></tbody></table></div><p class="fine" id="new-family-note"></p></div>
<div class="notice">Removing every source is a saved stress condition for the same selected candidate. Its score does not select a different winner or establish a universally robust fallback. New variants can have better isolated 2026 results and still fail to replace the validation-selected incumbent.</div></section>

<section id="leaders"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Validation selects · 2026 reports</p><h2>Nine retained T-120 leaders</h2><p class="muted">These dated T-120 results retain 919/919 eligible completed games in 2024, 934/934 in 2025 and 755/755 in the observed 2026 test population. One additional archived 2024 row remains ungraded. Historical test exposure remains disclosed.</p>
<div class="controls"><label>Annual validation weights<select id="profile" aria-label="Annual validation weights"><option value="50/50">50/50 · primary</option><option value="40/60">40/60 · sensitivity</option><option value="30/70">30/70 · sensitivity</option><option value="20/80">20/80 · sensitivity</option><option value="10/90">10/90 · sensitivity</option></select></label><button id="download" type="button">Download this evidence</button></div><p id="profile-note" class="fine" aria-live="polite"></p>
<div class="card"><div class="table-wrap"><table class="leader-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Objective</th><th scope="col">Saved policy</th><th scope="col" class="num">2024 · 919/919</th><th scope="col" class="num">2025 · 934/934</th><th scope="col" class="num">Validation score</th><th scope="col" class="num">2026 · 755/755</th></tr></thead><tbody id="leader-rows"></tbody></table></div></div>
<div class="notice warn">Changing the validation ratio reuses the same annual predictions. It does not fit estimators, reweight training rows or select on 2026. Coverage of the known completed population does not certify the full official census, original live issuance or eligibility for production.</div>
<details><summary>Saved ranks of the primary policies under every ratio</summary><div class="table-wrap" style="margin-top:15px"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Objective</th><th scope="col" class="num">50/50</th><th scope="col" class="num">40/60</th><th scope="col" class="num">30/70</th><th scope="col" class="num">20/80</th><th scope="col" class="num">10/90</th></tr></thead><tbody id="rank-rows"></tbody></table></div><p class="fine">These are the current saved ranks of each 50/50 primary policy. All 45 profile/objective winners and their validation values are unchanged from the preceding V096 return.</p></details></section>

<section id="cpu"><p class="eyebrow">04 / Measured execution</p><h2>Parallel fitting and scoring.<br>No sustained utilization pass.</h2><p class="muted">Both finite fitting phases finished in less than three minutes. They have measured CPU and concurrency, but neither establishes the required 180-second sustained acceptance result. V096's earlier pass remains evidence for V096.</p>
<div class="grid"><article class="card"><h3>Average CPU-equivalent by phase</h3><div id="phase-bars"></div><div class="legend"><span>Optimizer</span><span class="prep">Preparation</span><span class="other">Other callback work</span><span class="serial">Scoring workers</span></div><p class="fine">CPU seconds divided by phase wall seconds, on a common 24-core scale. These whole-phase averages are descriptive; they do not replace a qualifying sustained interval.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Current acceptance result</h3><dl class="facts" id="gate-facts"></dl><p class="fine" id="gate-limit"></p></article></div>
<article class="card" style="margin-top:18px"><h3>Selected capacity, observed processes and concurrency</h3><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Phase</th><th scope="col" class="num">Admitted workers</th><th scope="col" class="num">Distinct fit PIDs</th><th scope="col" class="num">Peak concurrent fits</th><th scope="col" class="num">Dispatch elapsed</th><th scope="col" class="num">Optimizer CPU</th></tr></thead><tbody id="phase-rows"></tbody></table></div></article>
<div class="grid" style="margin-top:18px"><article class="card"><h3>Checkpointed parallel scoring</h3><dl class="facts" id="scoring-facts"></dl><p class="fine">Scoring CPU is separate from optimizer CPU. The prior 1,105 policy scores and forecast pins were verified and reused without new scoring tasks or forecast-partition decoding.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Queue and total cost</h3><dl class="facts" id="queue-facts"></dl><p class="fine" id="queue-definition"></p></article></div>
<details style="margin-top:18px"><summary>Why the final heartbeat is not extra fitting time</summary><p class="fine" style="margin-top:15px" id="heartbeat-note"></p></details></section>

<section id="sources"><p class="eyebrow">05 / Cached sources and honest gaps</p><h2>Source reuse is measured; coverage is still incomplete</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><h3>This invocation's source work</h3><dl class="facts" id="source-facts"></dl><p class="fine">The source producer's inventory and this invocation's actual decoding are different quantities. A completed qualification task is not proof that every historical source observation exists.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Current fixture coverage</h3><dl class="facts" id="population-facts"></dl><p class="fine">All 133 pending fixtures remain in the manifest. Ten have unresolved kickoff times and the frozen contexts retain ten missing feature rows per target. Missing observations remain explicit.</p></article></div>
<div class="notice warn">Native Kalshi, Polymarket Global and Polymarket US still need authenticated as-of source routes, exact contract adapters and rights. DraftKings and other permitted bookmaker data retain their own clocks and missingness. Reference coverage is not a scored predictive benchmark or evidence of original historical possession.</div>
<article class="card"><h3>Current T-60 and T-120 source coverage</h3><p class="fine">This source grid has been inspected for the current 2024/2025/2026 populations. T-60 source cells are available evidence for preparation; they do not establish a completed T-60 fitting or evaluation campaign.</p><div class="controls"><label>Pregame horizon<select id="coverage-horizon" aria-label="Current source coverage horizon"><option value="T60m">T-60 · next campaign</option><option value="T2h">T-120 · dated comparison</option></select></label><label>Season<select id="coverage-season" aria-label="Current source coverage season"><option>2026</option><option>2025</option><option>2024</option></select></label><label>Target<select id="coverage-target" aria-label="Current source coverage target"><option value="winner">Winner</option><option value="margin">Margin</option><option value="total">Total</option></select></label></div><div class="table-wrap"><table class="source-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Bookmaker / route</th><th scope="col" class="num">Qualified features</th><th scope="col" class="num">References</th><th scope="col" class="num">Original availability</th><th scope="col" class="num">Predictive baseline</th></tr></thead><tbody id="coverage-rows"></tbody></table></div><p class="fine" id="coverage-note"></p></article>
<details><summary>Earlier-history T-60 source coverage, separately scoped</summary><p class="fine" style="margin-top:15px">This inspected table covers 2020–2023 only. It counts bookmaker-game cells across source products, not unique covered games, and cannot establish 2024/2025 validation coverage or a working T-60 model.</p><div class="controls"><label>Historical season<select id="source-season" aria-label="Historical T-60 coverage season"><option>2023</option><option>2022</option><option>2021</option><option>2020</option></select></label><label>Target<select id="source-target" aria-label="Historical T-60 coverage target"><option value="winner">Winner</option><option value="margin">Margin</option><option value="total">Total</option></select></label></div><dl class="facts" id="historical-source-facts"></dl><p class="fine" id="source-note"></p></details></section>

<section id="next"><p class="eyebrow">06 / Preparation, not execution</p><h2>V098 remains a separate preparation step</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><h3 id="next-title">Next owner continuation</h3><p id="next-status" class="policy-name"></p><dl class="facts" id="next-facts"></dl><p class="digest" id="next-digest"></p><p class="fine">The next runner must resolve the latest verified state again at launch and reuse exact completed work. The owner executes the research command. Report preparation launches no research or source retrieval.</p><p class="fine" id="next-runtime"></p></article><article class="card"><h3>What the completed tranche establishes</h3><p>The two new model families completed their registered source ablations, their missing-source stress outputs were retained, and the validation leaders held.</p><p>The wider V13 program is incomplete. The dated T-120 scorecards remain separate from any future T-60 campaign and from production deployment.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/tree/fbs/v093-launch-readiness-20261117/docs/fbs/v097">Read the preserved V096 / prepared V097 report</a></p></article></div><article class="card" style="margin-top:18px"><h3>Remaining scientific scope</h3><div id="remaining-branches"></div></article></section>

<section id="custody"><p class="eyebrow">07 / Integrity and publication</p><h2>The verified partial return preserves resumption</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><h3>Actual bytes and their scope</h3><dl class="facts" id="storage-facts"></dl><p class="digest" id="return-digest"></p><p class="fine" id="summary-comparison"></p><p class="fine">The control ZIP is not all scientific storage. The 512 MiB limit applies to each transport part; it is not an aggregate science cap.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Source review only</h3><p>This bounded report contains aggregate results, coarse model descriptions and explicit limitations. Private recipes, weights, raw licensed arrays, complete candidate forecast grids and owner execution packages remain excluded.</p><p>Source publication, live website deployment, owner execution and production promotion have independent evidence. This prepared source remains unmerged and does not establish deployment.</p></article></div><details style="margin-top:18px"><summary>Inspected evidence digests</summary><div id="evidence-pins"></div><p class="fine">The download is the exact bounded evidence projection embedded here. Artifact hashes identify the inspected inputs; they do not publish the private payloads.</p></details></section>
</main><footer><p id="footer-note">This dated report is not a live process monitor.</p><a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/pull/391">Review source</a></footer>
<script id="report-data" type="application/json">__DATA__</script>
<script>
'use strict';
(async()=>{
const raw=document.getElementById('report-data').textContent, expected='__DATA_SHA256__';
const digest=Array.from(new Uint8Array(await crypto.subtle.digest('SHA-256',new TextEncoder().encode(raw)))).map(x=>x.toString(16).padStart(2,'0')).join('');
if(digest!==expected)throw Error('The embedded evidence does not match its verified digest.');
const d=JSON.parse(raw),a=d.execution,c=d.cpu,s=d.selection,p=d.population,n=d.next_preparation;
const $=id=>document.getElementById(id),text=(id,value)=>{$(id).textContent=value},num=v=>Number(v).toLocaleString('en-US'),sec=v=>Number(v).toFixed(3)+' s',cpu=v=>Number(v).toFixed(3)+' CPU-s',clock=v=>new Date(v).toLocaleString('en-US',{timeZone:'UTC',year:'numeric',month:'short',day:'2-digit',hour:'2-digit',minute:'2-digit',second:'2-digit',hour12:false})+' UTC';
const metric=(value,kind)=>kind==='accuracy'?(100*value).toFixed(4)+'%':Number(value).toFixed(6);
const objective=(target,kind)=>target[0].toUpperCase()+target.slice(1)+' '+({accuracy:'accuracy',brier:'Brier',log_loss:'log loss',mae:'MAE',rmse:'RMSE',crps:'CRPS'}[kind]);
const facts=(id,rows)=>{const out=$(id);out.replaceChildren();for(const [label,value]of rows){const div=document.createElement('div'),dt=document.createElement('dt'),dd=document.createElement('dd');dt.textContent=label;dd.textContent=value;div.append(dt,dd);out.append(div)}};
const cell=(row,label,value,cls='')=>{const td=document.createElement('td');td.dataset.label=label;td.className=cls;if(value instanceof Node)td.append(value);else td.textContent=value;row.append(td)};
text('closure-note','Verified resumable return observed '+clock(a.observed_at)+'. The current scientific status is partial; the full program is not complete.');
text('new-fits',num(a.new_model_fits));text('complete-jobs',a.completed_jobs+' / '+a.registered_jobs);text('fit-processes',Math.max(...c.phases.map(x=>x.max_concurrent_fits)));text('test-games',num(p.completed_test_games));
facts('actual-facts',[['Child / supervisor exit','0 / 0'],['Scientific program','Incomplete'],['Historical failed attempts',a.historical_failed_attempts],['Operationally finished attempts',a.operationally_finished_attempts],['Fully complete V13 attempts',a.fully_v13_complete_attempts],['Current failed fits',a.failed_fits]]);text('actual-clock',a.tally_scope+' Current run: '+a.run_id+'.');
facts('reuse-facts',[['Earlier frontier jobs preserved',num(a.retained_frontier_jobs)],['Earlier frontier jobs redispatched',a.retained_frontier_jobs_dispatched],['Exact fitted states reused',a.reused_fit_states],['Inherited policies without new grading',num(a.inherited_policies_reused_without_scoring)],['Emitted forecast rows incl. ungraded',num(a.new_prediction_rows)],['Completed scored rows',num(a.new_scored_prediction_rows)],['New blend forecast rows',a.new_blend_rows]]);
function renderNewFamily(){const family=$('new-family').value;const rows=s.new_family_best.filter(x=>x.family===family);$('new-family-rows').replaceChildren();for(const x of rows){const tr=document.createElement('tr');cell(tr,'Objective',objective(x.target,x.metric));cell(tr,'New variant',x.family+' · '+x.variant);cell(tr,'50/50 rank',x.primary_rank,'num');cell(tr,'Validation',metric(x.selection_score,x.metric),'num');cell(tr,'Sources absent',metric(x.all_source_absent_validation_score,x.metric),'num');cell(tr,'2026 report',metric(x.annual_values[2],x.metric),'num');$('new-family-rows').append(tr)}text('new-family-note','Best new '+family+' representative per objective, selected from validation only. Full-precision annual values and stress values are in the evidence download. Zero primary leader replacements; zero test-driven promotions.');}
$('new-family').addEventListener('change',renderNewFamily);renderNewFamily();
function renderLeaders(){const profile=$('profile').value;const rows=s.leaders.filter(x=>x.profile===profile);$('leader-rows').replaceChildren();for(const x of rows){const tr=document.createElement('tr');cell(tr,'Objective',objective(x.target,x.metric));const label=document.createElement('span');label.className='policy-name';label.textContent=x.family;const detail=document.createElement('span');detail.className='policy-detail';detail.textContent=x.feature_group+' · '+x.variant+' · '+x.policy_alias;label.append(detail);cell(tr,'Saved policy',label);cell(tr,'2024 · 919/919',metric(x.annual_values[0],x.metric),'num');cell(tr,'2025 · 934/934',metric(x.annual_values[1],x.metric),'num');cell(tr,'Validation score',metric(x.selection_score,x.metric),'num');cell(tr,'2026 · 755/755',metric(x.annual_values[2],x.metric),'num');$('leader-rows').append(tr)}const different=rows.filter(x=>!x.same_policy_as_primary).length;text('profile-note',profile==='50/50'?'Primary: equal annual validation weights. Accuracy is higher-is-better; other objectives are lower-is-better. All nine primary winners remain unchanged from V096.':'Sensitivity '+profile+': '+different+' winner(s) differ from the 50/50 primary. Every winner matches the preceding saved result. Unchanged predictions; zero sensitivity refits; 2026 does not select the result.');}
$('profile').addEventListener('change',renderLeaders);renderLeaders();for(const x of s.leaders.filter(x=>x.profile==='50/50')){const tr=document.createElement('tr');cell(tr,'Objective',objective(x.target,x.metric));for(const profile of s.profiles){const row=s.leaders.find(y=>y.profile===profile&&y.target===x.target&&y.metric===x.metric);cell(tr,profile,row.primary_policy_rank,'num')}$('rank-rows').append(tr)}
const bar=(label,wall,values)=>{const div=document.createElement('div');div.className='phase';const head=document.createElement('div');head.className='phase-head';const name=document.createElement('span'),value=document.createElement('strong'),track=document.createElement('div');name.textContent=label;const cores=values.reduce((sum,x)=>sum+x[1],0)/wall;value.textContent=cores.toFixed(2)+' cores';head.append(name,value);track.className='bar-track';track.setAttribute('role','img');track.setAttribute('aria-label',label+': '+cores.toFixed(3)+' average CPU-equivalent cores on a 24-core scale');for(const [kind,seconds]of values){const part=document.createElement('span');part.className='bar '+kind;part.style.width=100*seconds/wall/c.hard_ceiling+'%';track.append(part)}div.append(head,track);$('phase-bars').append(div)};
for(const x of c.phases){bar(x.label+' dispatch',x.dispatch_wall_seconds,[['fit',x.optimizer_cpu_seconds],['prepare',x.preparation_cpu_seconds],['other',x.other_callback_cpu_seconds]]);const tr=document.createElement('tr');cell(tr,'Phase',x.label);cell(tr,'Admitted workers',x.admitted_workers,'num');cell(tr,'Distinct fit PIDs',x.observed_fit_processes,'num');cell(tr,'Peak concurrent fits',x.max_concurrent_fits,'num');cell(tr,'Dispatch elapsed',sec(x.dispatch_wall_seconds),'num');cell(tr,'Optimizer CPU',cpu(x.optimizer_cpu_seconds),'num');$('phase-rows').append(tr)}
bar('Parallel scoring workers',c.scoring.batch_wall_seconds_sum,[['serial',c.scoring.worker_cpu_seconds]]);
facts('gate-facts',[['Current sustained pass','Not established'],['Required interval',c.required_interval_seconds+' seconds'],['Validation dispatch',sec(c.phases[0].dispatch_wall_seconds)],['Frozen-test dispatch',sec(c.phases[1].dispatch_wall_seconds)],['Final remaining jobs','0 in both phases'],['Earlier pass saved in this run','None']]);text('gate-limit',c.short_work_reason+' Final status: '+c.current_gate_status+'. A count of 24 distinct PIDs does not mean 24 simultaneous fits.');
facts('scoring-facts',[['Completed scoring tasks',c.scoring.completed_tasks],['Batch elapsed times combined',sec(c.scoring.batch_wall_seconds_sum)],['Scoring worker CPU',cpu(c.scoring.worker_cpu_seconds)],['Coordinator outer elapsed',sec(c.scoring.coordinator_wall_seconds)],['Coordinator CPU',cpu(c.scoring.coordinator_cpu_seconds)],['Optimizer occupancy claimed','No']]);
facts('queue-facts',[['Prepared-ready high watermarks',c.phases.map(x=>x.prepared_ready_high_watermark).join(' / ')],['Preparation pending with idle slots',c.phases.map(x=>sec(x.preparation_pending_with_idle_slots_seconds)).join(' / ')],['Legacy preparation-not-ready measure',c.phases.map(x=>sec(x.preparation_not_ready_seconds)).join(' / ')],['Whole supervised invocation',(d.cost.whole_invocation_wall_seconds/60).toFixed(2)+' min'],['Final full-host compute estimate','$'+d.cost.estimated_full_host_usd.toFixed(6)],['Earlier science-stage estimate','$'+d.cost.science_stage_estimate_usd.toFixed(6)],['Compute guard','$'+d.cost.guard_usd]]);
text('queue-definition','Validation / frozen test are shown separately. The legacy not-ready measure includes busy preparation and is not pure starvation. The full-host estimate is through '+clock(d.cost.measured_at)+', not an invoice. Subphase estimates are already included in that total.');
text('heartbeat-note','The final live event was '+c.last_live_event+' at '+clock(c.last_live_timestamp)+', while its inherited pipeline observation remained '+clock(c.last_live_pipeline_observed_at)+'. Its zero-active-work state and stale fitting label do not extend the measured fit interval or replace the supervisor closure evidence.');
facts('source-facts',[['Current qualification jobs',d.sources.current_qualification_jobs_completed+' / '+d.sources.current_qualification_jobs_registered],['Qualified shards reused',num(d.sources.current_shards_reused)],['New shard conversions',d.sources.current_new_shard_conversions],['Rows decoded from that cache',d.sources.current_normalized_rows_decoded],['Historical jobs reused',d.sources.historical_jobs_reused+' / '+d.sources.historical_jobs_registered],['Official census requests',d.sources.new_cfbd_calls],['New paid odds requests',d.sources.new_paid_odds_calls],['New market-provider requests',d.sources.new_market_provider_requests]]);
facts('population-facts',[['2024 completed / observed fixtures',p.season_completed_counts['2024']+' / '+p.season_fixture_counts['2024']],['2025 completed / observed fixtures',p.season_completed_counts['2025']+' / '+p.season_fixture_counts['2025']],['2026 completed / pending',p.completed_test_games+' / '+p.pending_test_games],['Policies scoring every known completed game',num(p.test_policies_with_full_known_completed_coverage)+' / '+num(p.test_policy_count)],['Official/postseason completeness','Unproven'],['Pending feature gaps per target',p.frozen_context_pending_feature_gaps_per_target]]);
function renderHistoricalSource(){const year=Number($('source-season').value),target=$('source-target').value;const x=d.sources.historical_t60.find(x=>x.season===year&&x.target===target);facts('historical-source-facts',[['Observed completed-game denominator',x.expected_n_values.join(' / ')],['Bookmaker/product rows',x.bookmaker_rows],['Qualified bookmaker-game cells',num(x.qualified_feature_cells)],['Reference bookmaker-game cells',num(x.reference_cells)],['Qualified predictive-baseline cells',num(x.predictive_baseline_cells)],['Strict original-availability cells',num(x.strict_original_cells)]]);text('source-note',year+' '+target+' at T-60. These source-cell totals are not unique games and do not establish original quote possession or scored provider accuracy.');}
$('source-season').addEventListener('change',renderHistoricalSource);$('source-target').addEventListener('change',renderHistoricalSource);renderHistoricalSource();
const sourceNames={draftkings:'DraftKings',kalshi:'Kalshi',polymarket:'Polymarket Global',polymarket_us:'Polymarket US'},sourceRoutes={the_odds_api_v4:'The Odds API',kalshi_native:'Native Kalshi',polymarket_native:'Native Polymarket',polymarket_us_native:'Native Polymarket US'};
function renderCurrentSources(){const horizon=$('coverage-horizon').value,year=Number($('coverage-season').value),target=$('coverage-target').value,rows=d.sources.completed_horizon_coverage.filter(x=>x.horizon===horizon&&x.season===year&&x.target===target),first=['draftkings','kalshi','polymarket','polymarket_us'];rows.sort((a,b)=>(first.includes(a.bookmaker)?first.indexOf(a.bookmaker):99)-(first.includes(b.bookmaker)?first.indexOf(b.bookmaker):99)||a.bookmaker.localeCompare(b.bookmaker));$('coverage-rows').replaceChildren();for(const x of rows){const tr=document.createElement('tr');tr.dataset.bookmaker=x.bookmaker;const label=document.createElement('span'),route=document.createElement('span');label.className='policy-name';label.textContent=sourceNames[x.bookmaker]||x.bookmaker;route.className='policy-detail';route.textContent=sourceRoutes[x.source_route]||x.source_route;label.append(route);cell(tr,'Bookmaker / route',label);cell(tr,'Qualified features',x.feature_qualified_n+' / '+x.expected_n,'num');cell(tr,'References',x.reference_n+' / '+x.expected_n,'num');cell(tr,'Original availability',x.strict_original_availability_qualified_n+' / '+x.expected_n,'num');cell(tr,'Predictive baseline',x.predictive_baseline_qualified_n+' / '+x.expected_n,'num');$('coverage-rows').append(tr)}text('coverage-note','Current source matrix: '+num(d.sources.coverage_rows)+' cells across '+d.sources.bookmakers.length+' products and '+d.sources.horizons.length+' horizons. Inspected snapshot '+clock(d.sources.coverage_as_of)+'; qualification boundary '+clock(d.sources.qualification_boundary)+'. Every row retains the same completed-game denominator.');}
for(const id of ['coverage-horizon','coverage-season','coverage-target'])$(id).addEventListener('change',renderCurrentSources);renderCurrentSources();
text('next-status',n.status==='PREPARED_NOT_EXECUTED'?'Installed and native-verified · owner execution pending':n.status==='IN_PREPARATION'?'Replacement under preparation · owner execution pending':'Next scope and sealed runner evidence pending');
const nextGate=n.campaign_runtime_acceptance;text('next-runtime','Finite job completion and '+nextGate.record+' are separate. Campaign acceptance is '+nextGate.current_acceptance+' until a genuine, authenticated current-work window meets at least '+nextGate.required_representative_seconds+' seconds and '+(100*nextGate.required_minimum_useful_occupancy)+'% useful CPU occupancy. Adding shorter family waves cannot establish a pass. No T-60 runtime acceptance has been observed in this preparation.');
facts('next-facts',[['Release',n.release],['Scientific scope',n.planned_scope||'Pending sealed preparation'],['Planned registered jobs',n.planned_jobs===null?'Not yet sealed':num(n.planned_jobs)],['Planned raw/calibrated policies',n.planned_raw_calibrated_policies],['Planned fixed blend policies',n.planned_fixed_blend_policies],...n.branches.map(x=>[x.label+' · planned jobs',x.jobs]),['Scientific worker target / ceiling',n.target_workers+' / '+n.worker_ceiling],['Completed work','Preserve and verify before reuse'],['Owner executions from preparation',n.owner_runs_launched],['Native verification',n.native_verified?'Verified '+clock(n.native_verified_at):'Not yet established']]);text('next-digest',n.canonical_sha256?'Canonical SHA-256 '+n.canonical_sha256:'An executable hash and installed claim will appear only after the new canonical has been sealed and verified.');
for(const x of d.remaining_work){const row=document.createElement('div');row.className='branch';const head=document.createElement('div');head.className='branch-head';const title=document.createElement('strong'),pill=document.createElement('span'),detail=document.createElement('p');title.textContent=x.topic;pill.className='pill warn';pill.textContent=x.status.replaceAll('_',' ');head.append(title,pill);detail.textContent=x.detail;row.append(head,detail);$('remaining-branches').append(row)}
facts('storage-facts',[['Verified control ZIP',(d.storage.control_zip_bytes/1048576).toFixed(2)+' MiB · '+num(d.storage.control_zip_bytes)+' bytes'],['New separately uploaded payload bytes',(d.storage.new_uploaded_payload_bytes/1e9).toFixed(3)+' GB'],['New unique payloads',num(d.storage.new_unique_payload_count)],['Inherited bytes not recopied',(d.storage.inherited_payload_bytes_not_recopied/1e9).toFixed(3)+' GB'],['Logical payload count',num(d.storage.logical_payload_count)],['Maximum transport part','512 MiB'],['Aggregate science cap','None']]);text('return-digest','Return SHA-256 '+d.storage.control_zip_sha256);text('summary-comparison','Observed run-summary record sizes: V096 '+num(d.storage.previous_v096_run_summary_bytes)+' bytes; V097 '+num(d.storage.current_run_summary_bytes)+' bytes. This is a summary-record comparison, not the total scientific-storage size. Full pinned records remain in the resumption evidence.');
for(const pin of d.evidence){const row=document.createElement('div');row.className='pin';const title=document.createElement('strong'),hash=document.createElement('code');title.textContent=pin.label+' · '+num(pin.bytes)+' bytes';hash.textContent=pin.sha256;row.append(title,hash);$('evidence-pins').append(row)}
$('download').addEventListener('click',()=>{const blob=new Blob([JSON.stringify(d,null,2)+'\n'],{type:'application/json'}),url=URL.createObjectURL(blob),link=document.createElement('a');link.href=url;link.download='FBS_V098_PUBLIC_EVIDENCE.json';link.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(url),2000)});text('footer-note','Verified actual return observed '+clock(d.execution.observed_at)+'. This dated report preserves completed work and unfinished science. It is not a live process monitor.');
$('report').hidden=false;document.documentElement.dataset.ready='true';
})().catch(error=>{const target=document.getElementById('error');target.textContent='Evidence could not be verified: '+String(error.message||error);target.hidden=false;document.getElementById('report').hidden=true;document.documentElement.dataset.ready='error';});
</script></body></html>
